Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> set_decl
Rule 1     set_decl -> LBRACE RBRACE
Rule 2     set_decl -> LBRACE members RBRACE
Rule 3     members -> NUMBER
Rule 4     members -> members COMMA NUMBER

Terminals, with rules where they appear

COMMA                : 4
LBRACE               : 1 2
NUMBER               : 3 4
RBRACE               : 1 2
error                :

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

members              : 2 4
set_decl             : 0

Parsing method: LALR

state 0

    (0) S' -> . set_decl
    (1) set_decl -> . LBRACE RBRACE
    (2) set_decl -> . LBRACE members RBRACE

    LBRACE          shift and go to state 2

    set_decl                       shift and go to state 1

state 1

    (0) S' -> set_decl .



state 2

    (1) set_decl -> LBRACE . RBRACE
    (2) set_decl -> LBRACE . members RBRACE
    (3) members -> . NUMBER
    (4) members -> . members COMMA NUMBER

    RBRACE          shift and go to state 3
    NUMBER          shift and go to state 5

    members                        shift and go to state 4

state 3

    (1) set_decl -> LBRACE RBRACE .

    $end            reduce using rule 1 (set_decl -> LBRACE RBRACE .)


state 4

    (2) set_decl -> LBRACE members . RBRACE
    (4) members -> members . COMMA NUMBER

    RBRACE          shift and go to state 6
    COMMA           shift and go to state 7


state 5

    (3) members -> NUMBER .

    RBRACE          reduce using rule 3 (members -> NUMBER .)
    COMMA           reduce using rule 3 (members -> NUMBER .)


state 6

    (2) set_decl -> LBRACE members RBRACE .

    $end            reduce using rule 2 (set_decl -> LBRACE members RBRACE .)


state 7

    (4) members -> members COMMA . NUMBER

    NUMBER          shift and go to state 8


state 8

    (4) members -> members COMMA NUMBER .

    RBRACE          reduce using rule 4 (members -> members COMMA NUMBER .)
    COMMA           reduce using rule 4 (members -> members COMMA NUMBER .)
